<title>PORTUGAL: Yield rises on Portuguese 364-day bills.</title>
<headline>Yield rises on Portuguese 364-day bills.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield rose to 5.3811 percent, from 5.2835 percent previously, at the Treasury's sale of 364-day bills, the Bank of Portugal said.</p>
<p>The Treasury placed 26 billion escudos.</p>
<p>--LISBON BUREAU 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
